WITH q AS (
  INSERT INTO questions (section, topic, subtopic, question_text, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, foundation, content_category, discipline, cognitive_skill, estimated_time_seconds)
  VALUES ('bio_biochem', 'The Musculoskeletal System', 'Sarcomere Structure', 'A histologist examines a single skeletal-muscle myofibril by electron microscopy and identifies one repeating band that contains only thin (actin) filaments and has a single dense transverse line running through its center. Which band, and which line bisecting it, is the histologist most likely viewing?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "The A band, bisected by the Z-line"}, {"label": "B", "text": "The I band, bisected by the Z-line"}, {"label": "C", "text": "The I band, bisected by the M line"}, {"label": "D", "text": "The H zone, bisected by the M line"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'This is a Biology question that falls under the content category ''Organ Systems.'' The answer is B because the I band is the region that contains only thin (actin) filaments, and it is the I band—not any other band—that has a Z-line (Z disc) running through its middle. The textbook states that "The I band contains only thin filaments" while "Thick filaments occur only in the A band of a myofibril," so a band holding only thin filaments must be the I band. It further states that "Each I band has a dense line running vertically through the middle called a Z disc or Z line," which identifies the bisecting transverse line as the Z-line. (Choice A) The A band is wrong because thick filaments occur only in the A band, so it is not a thin-filament-only region; the A band is also not the band bisected by the Z-line, which instead runs through the middle of each I band. (Choice B) The I band is correct: it spans the entire length over which thin filaments run and is the band whose center is marked by the dense Z-line, matching both clues in the situation. (Choice C) The I band is the right band, but the M line is the wrong bisecting line—the M line lies in the middle of the H zone, where accessory proteins hold thick filaments together, whereas the I band is bisected by the Z-line. (Choice D) The H zone is wrong because it is the central region of the A band that contains only thick filaments, not thin filaments, and it is bisected by the M line rather than fitting a thin-filament-only band. This is a Knowledge of Scientific Concepts and Principles question because you must recall the filament composition of the sarcomere bands and which transverse line bisects the I band.', 'medium', '3B', 'Organ Systems', 'biology', 1, 105)
  RETURNING id
)
